course: dictionary
lesson: 3199
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Energy is a word with several meanings. It can mean how lively and active you feel, what makes things move or heat up in science, or power from fuel, electricity, the sun or wind. Context tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «I have lots of energy» is about feeling lively and ready to play. «Every one of these machines swaps force for distance or speed; none of them gives energy for free» is about science, where energy is what makes things work.
explain: In «A hedgehog ... its whole body has slowed down to save energy», the clue is slowed down. Energy here means the body's stored fuel, which the hedgehog saves so it lasts through winter.
fact: Energy is what is needed to make things move, heat up, light up or change.
fact: Energy comes in forms: heat, light, sound, movement, electrical, and stored chemical energy in food and fuel.
fact: Energy cannot be made or destroyed; it only changes from one form to another.
fact: «Full of energy» means lively and active.
fact: Renewable energy from the sun, wind or water won't run out, as in «solar energy».
exercise: «Every one of these machines swaps force for distance or speed; none of them gives energy for free.» In this sentence, what is energy? | *Something needed to make things move or change | A feeling of being lively | A type of bill you pay each month | The name of a machine
exercise: Mia says, «I have lots of energy». What does it mean? | *She feels lively and ready to be active | She has lots of bills to pay | She has a battery in her pocket | She feels cold
exercise: Which of these is renewable energy? | Oil pumped from under the sea | *Wind | Gas burned in a cooker | Petrol from a tank
test: «A hedgehog curled up in a pile of leaves in winter may breathe only a few times a minute; its whole body has slowed down to save energy.» What does save energy mean here? | Wake up and go hunting | Hide its energy in a box | Run faster to keep warm | *Use up its stored fuel slowly so it lasts through winter
test: Which statement about energy is true? | Energy only comes from electricity | Energy can be destroyed when a battery runs out | Energy can be made from nothing | *Energy can change from one form to another
exam: «Because energy is lost at each step, there are always far fewer predators than plant-eaters.» Why are there fewer predators? | Predators only eat fruit | Predators are smaller than plant-eaters | *Energy is lost at each step, so less is left for predators | Plants stop growing in winter
